# The technical-graph module's example graph: test data, not ontology content (the decision of 2026-11-02, item 4).
# It never ships in the module's package. The regression runs competency questions 45 to 50 on it, and the
# module's tests check it against the module's shapes. It is kept as committed; no script rebuilds it.
# Every identifier is made up, in the scheme urn:kpi-store-example:, and every name is an example name
# (the host example-sources, the steps example_pipeline.*).
# 1.1.0 adds made-up records for questions 56 and 57: two tables on an earlier platform, each replaced by a silver
# table, and one job and one pipeline that write those silver tables.
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@prefix dp: <https://w3id.org/mpc/ontology/modules/data-product/> .
@prefix layer: <https://w3id.org/mpc/ontology/modules/data-product/layer/> .
@prefix measure: <https://w3id.org/mpc/ontology/modules/kpi/measure/> .
@prefix ns1: <https://w3id.org/mpc/ontology/modules/authority/> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix result: <https://w3id.org/mpc/ontology/modules/technical-graph/check-result/> .
@prefix skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix tg: <https://w3id.org/mpc/ontology/modules/technical-graph/> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

<urn:kpi-store-example:tech:check/built-objects-hold-rows> a tg:QualityCheck ;
